# UI theme & dialogs (HyperLocalMart web)

When building or changing any portal screen (buyer-web, vendor-portal, delivery-portal, super-admin):

## Theme — required

- Use existing CSS variables from `@hlm-theme` / portal tokens: `--bg`, `--bg-elevated`, `--text`, `--text-muted`, `--accent`, `--border`, `--danger`, `--radius-*`, `--font-display`, `--shadow-*`.
- Reuse shared components (`Button`, `Banner`, `Card`, `TextField`, `PortalShell`, theme dialogs) before inventing new chrome.
- Match the surrounding portal’s layout density and patterns; do not ship unstyled browser defaults for primary UX.
- Guests share the default theme; personal theme picker only after login (buyer/vendor).

## Dialogs / alerts — hard rules

- **Never** use `window.alert`, `window.confirm`, or `window.prompt` for product UX. They ignore theme and show “localhost says…”.
- Use themed modals (`ConfirmDialog`, `ReasonDialog`, or equivalent styled with theme tokens).
- Destructive actions need a clear keep/go-back action and an explicit confirm label (e.g. “Keep item” / “Yes, cancel item”).

## Checklist before finishing a new screen

1. Looks correct in light + current accent (and dark if the portal supports it).
2. No native browser dialogs for confirmations.
3. Interactive controls use shared `Button` / form fields where possible.
4. Loading, empty, and error states use existing Banner / Empty patterns.
5. Usable on a phone (~390px): one column, ≥44px taps, no desktop-only layout traps (see `mobile-first.mdc`).
